      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The angle ${30}^{∘}$ is special, and its sine has the value\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} & = \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
