    "q-28935": {
      "dom_id": "step-q28935",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡{0}^{∘}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The angles ${45}^{∘},$ ${30}^{∘}$ and ${0}^{∘}$ are special angles, and their trigonometric ratios have the values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}=1,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{0}^{∘}=0.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡{0}^{∘} & = \\\\ 1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{3+\\sqrt{3}}{3}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
