    "q-244571": {
      "dom_id": "step-q244571",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The angles of ${60}^{∘}$ and ${90}^{∘}$ are special, and their trigonometric ratios have values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘}=1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}+1 & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
