      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡{0}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The angles of ${0}^{∘},$ ${45}^{∘},$ and ${90}^{∘}$ are special, and their trigonometric ratios have values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘}=1,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{0}^{∘}=0,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡{0}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘} & = \\\\ 1+0-1 & = \\\\ 0. & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
